  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening access to protection services for refugees and other vulnerable people in mixed movements</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to strengthen access to protection services for refugees and other vulnerable people in mixed movements Darien Province and Ember&#xE1;-Wouna&#xE1;n indigenous territories. This UNHCR project provides multi-purpose cash assistance, legal assistance to asylum seekers. In addition, People in mixed movements in Darien and in indigenous Embera&#xE1;-Wouna&#xE1;n transit communities&#x2019; benefits from better reception conditions and receive reliable and life-saving information about the risks of crossing through Darien jungle. The project provides life-saving assistance to 162,000 individuals, including 84,240 men, 45,360 women and 32,400 children and 8,100 Persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
